<Docs title="Sourcing · unfinished.one" description="Where unfinished.one numbers come from and how their provenance is recorded. Draft, pending legal review." canonical="https://unfinished.one/sourcing">
  <h1>Sourcing and provenance</h1>
  <p class="note"><strong>Draft — pending legal review.</strong> This policy may change before the first public release.</p>

  <h2 id="rules">Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Record where every number came from.</strong> Each entry lists its basis: the source type, title, link where there is one, and who made any estimate.</li>
    <li><strong>Never copy a paywalled table.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Label estimates as estimates.</strong> An expert estimate is graded D and names its editor.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="types">Source types</h2>
  <p>From strongest to weakest:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Observed data.</strong> Opt-in and anonymized, published only as aggregates above a minimum sample size.</li>
    <li><strong>Public government documents.</strong> US federal documents, which are in the public domain, and Canadian municipal asset management plans (AMPs) and capital asset policies, cited value by value.</li>
    <li><strong>Standards.</strong> Referenced by clause number only, never by their text.</li>
    <li><strong>Open research.</strong> Only where its licence is compatible with CC BY 4.0.</li>
    <li><strong>Expert estimates.</strong> From named editors, labelled as such.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>How many sources agree, and of what type, sets the <a href="/about#confidence">confidence grade</a>.</p>
  <p>Every document the library cites today is listed on <a href="/sources">Sources</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>An observation never identifies an owner, building or address in public output. Observations are described by region and building type only.</p>

  <h2 id="reuse">What we take from a document</h2>
  <p>We take values, not text. From a municipal policy or plan we record each stated life and the page it is on, and describe the row in our own words: the component or system it covers. We do not republish a document's tables or wording, and we do not host copies of documents; every value links to the publisher's own file. Other sources are US federal works, which are in the public domain, or documents whose publisher allows reuse.</p>
  <h2 id="removal">Removal on request</h2>
  <p>If you publish a document we cite and would rather we did not, write to <a href="mailto:hello@unfinished.one">hello@unfinished.one</a> with the document's link. We will remove its values and publish new versions of the entries that cited it, usually within a week.</p>

  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a value is wrong, or a source is misrepresented or should not be used, write to <a href="mailto:hello@unfinished.one">hello@unfinished.one</a> with the entry link. Corrections are published as a new version; earlier versions stay at their permanent links.</p>
</Docs>
